# XSH rand() and srand()
# Copyright (c) 2026 Nicholas Martin. All rights reserved.
#
# rand_r() is not on this page in this edition (it was removed), so it is
# not tested. The generator's actual values are not specified, only its
# range and its repeatability.

assertion  XSH.rand.001
anchor     functions/rand.html#DESCRIPTION
anchor     functions/rand.html#RETURN VALUE
class      required
since      1988
says       RAND_MAX is at least 32767, and 1000 consecutive rand() values are
           all in the range 0 to RAND_MAX and are not all equal.
test       t/001-range.c

assertion  XSH.rand.002
anchor     functions/rand.html#DESCRIPTION
class      required
since      1988
says       Calling srand() again with the same seed makes rand() repeat the
           same 100 values, for seeds 1, 42, 0 and the largest unsigned
           value; srand() with one seed, then another, then the first
           again, also reproduces the first run.
test       t/002-repeat.c

assertion  XSH.rand.003
anchor     functions/rand.html#DESCRIPTION
class      required
since      1988
says       rand() called before any srand() gives the same sequence as after
           srand(1): 50 values taken first, then srand(1) and 50 more are
           equal.
note       Taken at the start of the process, before anything else could
           have seeded the generator.
test       t/003-default-seed.c
